1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Before he ever reached the roof,
Ahmed Çelebi had to make the wings work.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,800
He studied birds, measured the wind,
and tested every wooden joint.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,300
The first attempt was not heroic.
The angle was wrong, and the canvas folded.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,900
So he rebuilt the frame,
tightened the harness, and watched the ribbons.

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,400
This time, the wind pointed in one direction.
The wings finally agreed.

6
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:21,000
From the roof of Galata Tower,
Ahmed stepped forward—not down.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,700
The wing caught the air,
and the city opened beneath him.

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:28,400
According to Evliya Çelebi,
he crossed toward Üsküdar.

9
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,100
He was said to land
in Doğancılar Square.

10
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:36,200
History or legend, the image remains:
one inventor, one handmade wing, one enormous sky.

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:40,000
And for a few unforgettable seconds,
Istanbul became a place a man could fly across.

